SPEC §3, §4. Kubernetes::Comb::SVG::Cell with from_cr: accepts a CR-shaped hash or an object answering TO_JSON. Fields: name, namespace, class, phase (unknown string -> Unknown, original kept), enabled (false -> Disabled), depends_on, endpoints, borrowed + upstream context/via, group (from the configured label key), message (condition message when not Running). Missing status is fine; missing metadata.name is the only error. The facade's input handling (array, List with items, single CR) belongs here too. Tests with JSON fixtures under t/data/ for every row of the §3 table.

2026-10-02 02:08 Decisions in Cell (SPEC left them open):
- Unknown phase: phase is 'Unknown', the status.phase string is kept in raw_phase (undef when absent). Phases match exactly, case-sensitive.
- spec.enabled is tri-state as in the CRD: unset/null = on; JSON false, 0, '' and the string 'false' = off. Off wins over any status.phase (phase Disabled, raw_phase keeps the status value).
- message: every non-empty string in status.conditions[].message, in condition order, duplicates dropped, joined with newline; undef while phase is Running. No filtering by condition status.
- endpoints: [{ name, port }], port as string or undef; entries without a string name are dropped.
- borrowed: status.upstream is a non-empty hash. null, {} or a non-hash is not borrowed. upstream_context is a string or undef, upstream_via an array of strings (CRD: via is [Str]).
- dependsOn / via given as one string count as a one-element list; duplicates dropped, order kept. A self-reference is kept (cycle handling is Layout's).
- Nested objects answering TO_JSON are unwrapped at every level read (bounded, a TO_JSON returning itself cannot hang).
- cells_from(input, opts): array, hash with an items key (non-array items = empty), any other hash = one CR, undef = no cells. Returns a list in input order. Duplicate name: the first is kept, later ones dropped silently - identity is metadata.name per SPEC, and data-name must stay unique.
- Error: croak 'Kubernetes::Comb::SVG::Cell->from_cr: Comb without metadata.name' - also for an empty or non-string name and for an element that is not a CR at all. No element index in the message.
- cpanfile: Carp, Scalar::Util (runtime); JSON::MaybeXS, Path::Tiny (test).

